      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "There are 9 teams and each team plays 3 other teams twice, which means each game must be counted twice when we simply multiply the number of teams by the number of opponent teams and then divide by 2.\n\nTo account for the games played by each team with itself, we must subtract one from the result because the teams cannot play themselves. \n\n$9 \\cdot 3 = 27$ \n\n$27/2 = 13.5$ \n\nSince the number of games cannot be fractional, we must round down, but that ignores the fact that there is a team losing, becomes positive.\n\nSo we multiply 8 by 12 which will explain the reasons in the beginning.\n\nWrong, it should be $8 \\times 12 = 96$ as each game is counted twice, and there are $8$ game between each pair.\n\nHence, the answer is $\\boxed{11}$.\n\nWhat if I forgot that each pair of teams play 3 games? I remembered that the answer indeed doesn't depend on the number of games each pair plays.",
